# Advanced UI Agent

You are fixing and completing split-view, compact mode, and web side-panels for Mogwser. Most files exist — fix identified bugs.

## CRITICAL: Read Before Writing
Run `git log --oneline -10` first, then read every file before modifying.

## Key Fixes

### 1. Fix MogwserSplitView storage integration (MogwserSplitView.mjs:431-472)
The `_persistGroups()` and `_restoreFromStorage()` methods use `window.gMogwserWorkspaces.storage.set/get()` which doesn't exist. Fix by importing MogwserWorkspaceStorage directly:

```js
const { MogwserWorkspaceStorage } = ChromeUtils.importESModule(
  "chrome://mogwser/content/workspaces/MogwserWorkspaceStorage.mjs"
);
```

Then in `_persistGroups`:
```js
static async _persistGroups() {
  try {
    const data = MogwserSplitView._groups.map(g => ({
      id: g.id,
      tree: g.tree.serialize(),
      tabIds: [...g.tabIds],
    }));
    const stored = await MogwserWorkspaceStorage.load() || {};
    stored.splitGroups = data;
    MogwserWorkspaceStorage.save(stored, true);
  } catch (e) {
    console.error("MogwserSplitView: failed to persist groups:", e);
  }
}
```

And in `_restoreFromStorage`:
```js
static async _restoreFromStorage() {
  try {
    const stored = await MogwserWorkspaceStorage.load();
    if (!stored || !Array.isArray(stored.splitGroups)) return;
    // ... rest of existing logic using stored.splitGroups
  } catch (e) { ... }
}
```

### 2. Side-panel browser element
The current implementation uses an HTML `<iframe>` element. For chrome-privileged browsing in Firefox, `document.createXULElement('browser')` would be more appropriate. If changing this is too risky, add a code comment documenting the limitation.

## Existing Architecture
- Split tree: SplitLeafNode (tabId) and SplitNode (direction, children[])
- Positions calculated as CSS inset percentages
- Compact mode: `mogwser-compact` and `mogwser-compact-hover` attributes on sidebar
- CSS variable `--mogwser-compact-mode: 0|1`
- Side-panel: URL input, iframe browser, resize handle, quick-access picker
- Events: MogwserSplitViewChanged, MogwserCompactModeChanged on window

## Conventions
- ES modules (.mjs), static class singletons
- Globals: gMogwserSplitView, gMogwserCompactMode, gMogwserSidePanel
- CSS BEM naming
- CustomEvents on `window`

# Themes & Privacy Agent

You are fixing and completing the theme engine and privacy panel for Mogwser. Most files exist — fix gaps and add missing tests.

## CRITICAL: Read Before Writing
Run `git log --oneline -10` first, then read every file before modifying.

## Key Additions

### 1. Add rgbToHsl roundtrip test (tests/unit/test_theme_colors.js)
Add these test tasks at the end of the file:

```js
add_task(async function test_rgb_to_hsl_roundtrip_red() {
  const rgb = MogwserGradientPicker.hslToRgb(0, 100, 50);
  const hsl = MogwserGradientPicker.rgbToHsl(rgb.r, rgb.g, rgb.b);
  Assert.equal(hsl.h, 0, "Roundtrip red hue should be 0");
  Assert.equal(hsl.s, 100, "Roundtrip red saturation should be 100");
  Assert.equal(hsl.l, 50, "Roundtrip red lightness should be 50");
});

add_task(async function test_rgb_to_hsl_roundtrip_cyan() {
  const rgb = MogwserGradientPicker.hslToRgb(180, 50, 60);
  const hsl = MogwserGradientPicker.rgbToHsl(rgb.r, rgb.g, rgb.b);
  Assert.equal(hsl.h, 180, "Roundtrip cyan hue should be 180");
  // Allow ±1 for rounding
  Assert.ok(Math.abs(hsl.s - 50) <= 1, "Roundtrip cyan saturation should be ~50");
  Assert.ok(Math.abs(hsl.l - 60) <= 1, "Roundtrip cyan lightness should be ~60");
});
```

### 2. Add theme transition CSS
In `src/mogwser/themes/mogwser-themes.css`, ensure there is a rule for the double-buffer transition class:

```css
