Check if this already exists before adding.

### 3. Verify privacy prompt API
In MogwserPrivacyPanel._promptAddException (line ~594-611), the code calls `Services.prompt.prompt()` with wrong parameter count. The correct signature is:
```js
Services.prompt.prompt(window, title, text, {value: ""}, null, {})
```
where it returns boolean and mutates the {value} object.

## Existing Architecture
- Theme model: { id, name, type, colors: {primary, secondary, accent, background} (HSL), gradient, darkMode, metadata }
- CSS variable injection at :root
- Double-buffer transitions via `mogwser-theme-transitioning` class
- Privacy toggles: 5 entries in PRIVACY_TOGGLES array mapping to Firefox prefs
- Protection levels: strict (≥4 active), standard (≥2), minimal
- Per-site exceptions via Services.perms

## Conventions
- ES modules (.mjs), static class singletons
- Globals: gMogwserThemeEngine, gMogwserPrivacyPanel
- MogwserThemeChanged and MogwserCompactModeChanged events on window
- CSS BEM naming
- Tests: add_task pattern with Assert.ok/equal/deepEqual
